opening='Make a school-life photograph of a student character, capturing a moment of school life at the end of a baking practical. '
ref='Use the supplied photograph as a face-and-hair visual guide for a dark chin-length bob, separated wispy fringe, brown eyes and softly rounded facial contour. The adult woman is a fictional student character in this scene. '
room='School worktables, stools and a chalkboard bearing a simple baking diagram establish the home-economics classroom. A tray of golden bread sits on the workbench beside her. '
options={
'O1_waist_apron':opening+ref+'She wears a white blouse with folded sleeves, a navy neck ribbon and pleated navy uniform skirt. A waist-only apron begins at the belt and covers the skirt front; its upper edge leaves the blouse fully visible. Flour marks the apron where the workbench meets her waist. Her left hand steadies its front bow while her right hand pulls one loose end sideways, beginning to release the waist tie while the remaining loose belt still rests against her hips. '+room+'She keeps a relaxed standing balance and looks toward the completed bread with a small relieved smile. A vertical knees-up view from a gentle frontal three-quarter position holds face, both hands, fastening and bread together. Afternoon window light falls across the blouse, apron and table, making the practical layer and its current state readable. The photograph connects the completed class task to a modest release of effort through clothing and gesture.',
'O2_result_inspection':opening+ref+'She stands at her school workbench in a white blouse with sleeves folded to her elbows, navy neck ribbon and pleated navy skirt, with a pale blue bib apron tied securely at the waist. Both hands have paused on the workbench beside a tray of completed golden bread. Her fingertips rest lightly on the table, her chin is gently lowered and her gaze settles on the bread between her hands. The apron has flour marks from the practical, while the bread surface and nearby cleared workspace show the visible result. '+room+'A small smile and lowered shoulders make the moment quietly appealing, with the attention held on her work rather than the camera. A vertical environmental portrait from a gentle frontal three-quarter position includes her face, forearms, apron and tray. Soft afternoon window light connects her skin, cotton and workbench. Her still hands and the inspected result carry the transition into rest.',
'O3_seam_inspection':opening+ref+'At her school workbench she wears a white blouse with rolled cuffs, a navy ribbon and pleated navy skirt beneath a flour-marked pale blue bib apron. The apron remains fastened. Her left hand lifts a small edge of its own lower hem and folds it outward; her right fingers steady that fold so the inner seam finish can be seen next to the outer fabric. She studies the sewing with a faint interested smile. The coordinated blouse, ribbon and skirt remain visible as a consistent school uniform around this small practical layer. '+room+'Both arms bend easily close to her body. A vertical knees-up view preserves face, both hand contacts, folded garment edge and completed bread tray in the same frame. Afternoon window light gives the small turned edge enough separation from the hanging apron. The photograph treats a brief quality check of something she wears as a quiet school-room pause after class work.',
'O4_class_snapshot':opening+ref+'She stands beside the bread workbench in a white rolled-sleeve blouse, navy ribbon and pleated uniform skirt with a flour-marked pale blue bib apron over it. Both hands remain at its loosening front waist bow, one steadying the knot and the other drawing a loose tie outward. She briefly turns her face toward the photographer and offers a small relaxed smile, acknowledging a compact-camera classroom snapshot during this practical-class pause. '+room+'Her body remains balanced and both forearms connect clearly to the hands at the fastening. A vertical knees-up snapshot keeps the waist action and bread visible, with familiar fluorescent classroom illumination and a modest direct compact-camera flash creating an informal recorded-at-school feeling. The photograph keeps the completed task and apron action but makes the camera acknowledgement part of the moment.',
'O5_skirt_motion':opening+ref+'She wears the white school blouse, navy ribbon, pleated navy skirt and flour-marked pale blue apron, still tied at the waist. A short playful turn beside the workbench sends the lower skirt pleats into a modest arc. Both arms stay clear of the table; her torso turns through the hips while her head returns toward the completed bread, smiling lightly at the end of the practical. '+room+'The turning figure and the stationary bread tray create a contrast between a finished task and newly available movement. A vertical three-quarter-length photograph retains her face, connected arms, apron and the full moving skirt edge. Soft afternoon window light catches the pleat edges and flour on the apron, with the classroom fixtures remaining recognisable. This is a restrained school-life fashion motion moment with a clear work setting and an ordinary fictional subject.',
'O6_lantern_light':opening+ref+'The adult student stands at her workbench in a white blouse with sleeves folded to the elbows, navy ribbon and navy pleated skirt, wearing a flour-marked pale blue bib apron. Her left hand steadies its front waist knot while her right hand pulls one tie sideways; both grips and the slackened loop remain visible. A paper lantern hanging over the worktable supplies soft warm light that reaches her face, cotton apron and bread tray. '+room+'She glances toward the completed bread with a small relieved smile, while the lantern gives the classroom a quiet sheltered tone. A vertical knees-up frame from a gentle frontal three-quarter viewpoint shows face, both forearms, fastening and completed work together. The warm lantern glow becomes the main illumination; the school room remains legible behind the student and the practical-class relation remains ordinary and physically coherent.',
'O7_head_rest_stretch':opening+ref+'She stands beside the workbench in a white rolled-sleeve blouse, navy neck ribbon and pleated navy skirt beneath a flour-marked pale blue bib apron, still tied at the waist. Both hands rest behind her head for a brief post-task stretch. Her upper arms join her shoulders, elbows remain distinct to either side, and each forearm leads to its own hand behind the head; the fingers are partly hidden but their arm routes remain clear. Her shoulders relax and she smiles softly toward the completed bread. '+room+'The fixed apron and the lifted arms contrast completed work with a release of bodily tension. A vertical knees-up view from a gentle frontal three-quarter position retains her face, both elbow routes, uniform layers and bread tray. Soft afternoon window light links the cotton and class work surfaces, making a calm and modestly appealing school-life pause.'}
# All complete alternative prompts are authored after reading complete source meaning.
assess={
'O1_waist_apron':('cand_84609b6e97c25e949358057651ae1ea1','appearance, material, pose','The bare blouse front and waist-only layer expose the uniform ensemble more clearly. However, the release soon removes the only apron support, making the action a near-drop rather than the calmer work-to-break transition. The baseline bib remains supported while its waist relaxes and gives flour a broad readable work surface. Retain baseline on situational clarity and garment continuity, not because its apron type was requester-locked.'),
'O2_result_inspection':('cand_569ef0491e2d5be8b7c70a947908f9bc; cand_6cd933faa0655a93a50ae4b3a760a836','action, pose, expression, composition','The still hands and downward attention make inspection of the result clearer; this is a viable calm photograph at the same subtle appeal. It makes apron wearing state static, leaving the principal pose/clothing relationship to the generic work context. The baseline gives the hands their own legible practical action while keeping the result nearby. Prefer baseline for a stronger connection between garment state and the end of class. The school-appearance source is not natively qualified and no full-source adoption is claimed.'),
'O3_seam_inspection':('cand_17e89ecffe7e5634b84e66e15af751f4; cand_7fe9e0deadb45888b23a1212cf3f214a','action, appearance, pose','This makes garment construction especially readable and gives both hands a clear common target. It is coherent as a brief self-inspection, but seam quality and bread completion compete as two tasks; the photograph needs a second reason for inspecting the seam. Baseline clothing release follows directly from completed class work and has a cleaner cause-response hierarchy. Prefer baseline for emotional credibility and unity; seam inspection is compatible but less useful here.'),
'O4_class_snapshot':('cand_21d0e2b88e91558fb2babb334969e486','action, expression, lighting, style','Camera acknowledgement would establish a familiar class snapshot and show the face more directly. Its fluorescent-plus-flash recording style shifts the moment toward a keepsake pose, and looking at the camera weakens the relationship to the bread. The baseline keeps the viewer close to an unguarded task transition with motivated window light. Prefer baseline for connected attention and quiet presence, while recognising that a posed class snapshot is a valid school-life direction.'),
'O5_skirt_motion':('cand_8991868ea80e52829549b60f7fdf4704','action, pose, composition','The turn gives a livelier silhouette and readable pleat motion, with a credible end-of-task playfulness. The torso motion and swinging skirt become the dominant event, while the apron remains static and the bread becomes a contextual prop. At creativity one, the baseline is the more specific clothing-state transition tied to this practical; choose it for hierarchy and purpose rather than treating movement as prohibited.'),
'O6_lantern_light':('cand_df25c36140fe590db05da8609ff70e57','lighting, atmosphere','The paper glow could support intimate warmth while preserving the apron action and class result. It introduces a visually salient light fixture whose school-room purpose is unspecified and makes the moment feel decorated. The baseline window light belongs to the room without a competing object, and keeps flour and uniform clearer. Prefer baseline for setting credibility and restrained scene direction; warmth itself is already realised.'),
'O7_head_rest_stretch':('cand_5cda074fcfe050f88f37ec20bd8580dd','pose, action','This replaces a fine hand fastening with a broad readable release of bodily tension, a viable post-class pause. The partly hidden hands still have coherent elbow ownership, but their useful relation to clothing disappears and the apron is only costume context. The baseline lets both hands explain a particular garment state and keeps the small relief tied to a completed task. Prefer baseline for the appearance/pose test purpose, not an invented universal ban on hidden hands.')}
findings=[
('redundancy_and_native_prerequisite','The source preserves one declared adult arm from shoulder through elbow, wrist and hand without selecting a pose. The baseline already requires two visible forearms and each own hand on the apron; its frozen embodiment review traces ownership and reach. No distinct artistic change is supplied. Its already-declared biological-arm prerequisite has no new requester-grounded native witness and will not be retrofitted.'),
('compatible_not_preferred','Uniform component inspection covers coordinated cut, colour and trim, not unfastening. O3 realises an actual seam/ensemble check after practical class. It is compatible but splits attention between seam quality and bread completion; baseline wins the common clarity/purpose comparison.'),
('unestablished_meaning','The complete source makes an apron tie a cover-identity clue. A school practical apron is established; covert identity is not. Treating the mere tie as that clue would invent an unsupported meaning and the source supplies no concrete discriminating identity relation. Skip without borrowing its clue.'),
('native_bundle_unavailable','The compound combines a bounded skirt side opening revealing one continuous leg with face-and-garment co-framing, and its selected components must remain complete. Existing frozen owners and qualified child selections are not available for this whole cue. A bib apron also covers the skirt front; a side-opening emphasis adds no practical-class transition. Do not cherry-pick face framing as an adoption of the bundle.'),
('reference_and_case_scope','C05 is a tie-knot/lower-collar close crop explicitly placing the rest of the face outside the frame, with fingertip contacts retained. It is a complete new school-appearance source, not a generic waist-knot tip. It would remove the face/hair reference assessment and completed-work relation from this declared case. The source is not natively qualified. No adopted detail; the baseline front-waist action predates this source.'),
('already_realised','The bundle keeps existing garment construction, recognisable everyday place and one practical illumination on both. Baseline already has the uniform and worn apron in a home-economics room under window light reaching face and cotton. No distinct change is needed. Its optional member/profile is not selected and no native authority is inferred.'),
('compatible_not_preferred','The complete source is a waist-only apron beginning at the belt, with no chest bib or shoulder straps. O1 tests that whole garment choice as a coherent independent generic variation. It shows the blouse better, but loses the supported bib transition and larger flour surface; baseline preferred after comparison. No waist-only effect is retained.'),
('context_mismatch','Opening a parcel at a home table includes the person, opened flaps, contents connected to packaging, hand contact and supported box. Neither parcel nor home scene belongs to this practical. Copying only its generic state-change relation would not be source adoption; the baseline already independently connects apron action and slackening result.'),
('native_unqualified_and_scene_displacement','F03 is a full gym boxing guard: padded fists beside cheeks, bent elbows at ribs, staggered feet on a mat. It is new school-appearance material but natively unqualified. It would replace the work task with gym practice rather than clarify this local classroom action; no boxing component is retained.'),
('unmet_context_requirement','The complete contextual option loosens a trouser belt after arrival home while trousers stay worn. Its own conditions require mentioned place/garments outside declared changes already established. No home arrival or trousers are frozen, and effects do not permit a new setting. An apron tie cannot substitute for the belt buckle.'),
('unmet_primary_requirement','The pantry table source specifically keeps remaining supply and all destination portions together and requires household_food_depletion_portioning_event. This scene has completed bread, not household scarcity/portion allocation. Do not convert bread presence into a depletion narrative.'),
('compatible_not_preferred','The source pauses hands beside a completed section while the adult inspects it; no hidden desire is established. O2 puts both hands beside the bread and gaze on its surface. It gives clearer result inspection but makes the garment state static; baseline preferred for the direct pose-clothing relation.'),
('new_source_not_adopted','T06 requires fine pale dust on a dark apron with denser accumulation at the waist crease and visible underlying weave. Baseline independently had flour on a pale blue apron before retrieval; that is not adoption of this complete dark-apron crease/weave realization. The natively-unqualified source supplies no whole-source authority. Keep original broad work trace; do not claim its microstructure or change colour merely to use it.'),
('compatible_not_preferred','The wearer folds a small edge of their own garment to show the inner seam; actor and apron are established. O3 realises both hands supporting that fold. It is a plausible quality check but adds a competing task to the bread result; baseline is the more causally economical pause.'),
('unmet_profile_evidence','The achievement-reward profile needs personally verified readable success, mostly symmetric cheek/lip movement, result-directed eyes and a released control or collaborator response. Its exact success evidence names a working/restored device, passing test or repaired functioning object. Bread beside a small smile does not supply that whole profile. Do not promote a general relieved smile to this specialized success proof.'),
('unmet_primary_requirement','The non-text achievement marker belongs to a public_recognition_bid and requires that primary context. Here no audience or public recognition attempt is established. The bread is already a concrete class result, but it does not grant a recognition-bid narrative.'),
('already_realised','The environmental portrait source keeps adult, functional place, related task fixtures and enough surrounding space in one frame. Baseline literally retains face, forearms, waist fastening and bread tray with school worktables and chalkboard. It is already an environmental relation, with no distinct added staging supplied; no new source effect retained.'),
('compatible_not_preferred','The complete bilingual source is a posed compact-digicam classroom snapshot under fluorescent light. O4 develops that recording relation with direct camera acknowledgement while keeping apron action. It makes a credible keepsake but weakens attention to the completed work; the baseline observational relation wins.'),
('irrelevant_axes','Back width and posterior muscle depth are separate body-geometry axes. Neither axis distinguishes the requested school appearance/pose topic in this selected garment transition, and no regional body change is needed. Their word overlap does not support an apron or school action. Skip without changing body shape.'),
('unrelated_object','The canonical crossbow source requires stock, transverse prod, string, bolt track and release mechanism; an ordinary bow cannot substitute. No weapon is part of this class task. No source effect permits attaching this object to the practical merely because broad topic retrieval returned it.'),
('no_distinct_supported_change','The diegetic scene-register source centres functioning institutions/exchange/evidence rather than costume posing. Baseline already shows a functional class task and result instead of an isolated costume display. The source supplies no particular new local institution operation to realize here and no effects; avoid inventing a wider evidence system.'),
('compatible_not_preferred','The source is a spinning-skirt motion pose, not fastening work. O5 realises the modest skirt turn as a complete school-life photo. It is lively but the moving silhouette displaces the garment-state transition; baseline wins the common purpose/hierarchy comparison.'),
('unmet_existing_garment_requirement','The contextual source supports part of a long hem in one hand while the rest falls naturally. Its conditions require the long garment already established outside its action/pose effects. A pleated uniform skirt is frozen without a long hem, and both current hands have a separate fastening action. Do not infer or lengthen a hem to make this source fit.'),
('unmet_weapon_context','The English RPG-ready stance and Korean armed-ready wording together imply a prepared weapon/cosplay action. No weapon or RPG event is established and its effects only declare action. Do not introduce a weapon or recast an apron tool as one.'),
('compatible_not_preferred','The source is actual interior glow from a paper lantern, not simply any warm grade. O6 introduces that coherent light source. The fixture competes with the practical context and needs a separate setting rationale; baseline window light gives shared warmth with fewer competing cues.'),
('compatible_not_preferred','The source puts both hands behind/under the head with continuous shoulder-elbow routes and distinct elbow ownership. O7 realises a standing post-task stretch using the behind-head branch. It gives broad relaxation but removes the hands from the clothing transition; baseline wins the appearance/pose relation comparison.'),
('new_source_comparison_not_adoption','E02 requires chin dipped toward chest, eyes directed to the desk beneath the student hands. O2 explores that downward task-inspection direction with hands at the worktable. Baseline instead has hands at waist and a glance toward bread; those are not E02. The source is natively unqualified, and its full desk/hand relation is not retained.'),
('native_profile_not_selected','This hair-bow variant requires two actual loops at one knot fixed into the same wearer hair, with visible attachment and strict gate. A neck ribbon and apron bow have different owners and cannot substitute. No hair-bow profile/owner is selected; adding that small attachment would compete with the functional waist knot without advancing the practical. Source has no independent native authority.'),
('unmet_object_and_layer_context','The complete towel variant requires both hands gripping one towel upper edge, continuous front drape over torso/pelvis, and a separate swimsuit behind with a small strap window. Towel and swimsuit are not established. Do not substitute the worn apron for a held towel or keep only the two-hand metaphor.'),
('new_source_not_adopted','Q05 is a seated student with shoulders forward, elbows close to ribs and hands together above knees. It is a complete natively-unqualified school pose. It would remove both hands from the apron and replace the work-to-break fastening event with an inward seated silhouette. No isolated elbow cue is borrowed; the baseline waist-height elbow position was independently authored.'),
('locked_subject_and_biography','The source changes subject to an adult alumni school-uniform reference model. Frozen subject meaning is a student character; the reference establishes no alumni biography. The fictional adult portrayal does not verify alumni status and subject is locked. No adoption or factual claim about the person.')]
assert len(findings)==len(rows)
reviews=[];decisions=[]
for ix,(row,(kind,reason)) in enumerate(zip(rows,findings),1):
 r=row['source']; review={'review_id':f'S{ix:02d}','candidate_id':r['candidate_id'],'realization_id':r['realization_id'],'source_sha256':r['source_sha256'],'queries':row['queries'],'finding':kind,'complete_source_review':reason,'final_use':'skip','native_whole_source_adopted':False,'new_school_appearance_source':(r['native'].get('research_semantics') or {}).get('schema')=='photo-school-life-visual-semantics/v1'}
 reviews.append(review)
 for q in row['queries']:
  decisions.append({'slot':q,'candidate_id':r['candidate_id'],'realization_id':r['realization_id'],'source_sha256':r['source_sha256'],'use':'skip','rationale':f"S{ix:02d} in composition-comparison.md: {reason} Final retained option B0; this occurrence contributes no new retained effect."})
(b/'source-reviews.json').write_text(json.dumps(reviews,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2)+'\n')
lines=['# Arm A composition comparison','',f'Baseline path: {s["artifacts"]["baseline"]["path"]}',f'Baseline SHA-256: {hashlib.sha256(base.encode()).hexdigest()}','Frozen creativity: 1. Compare restrained local replacement, subtraction and addition at sensual 1, fetish 0, surreal 0; no candidate quota and no automatic preference for the first wording.','Requester invariants: school-life photograph, student character, school-life moment. Reference-use scope remains visible face/hair guidance, without real age/identity/personality claims. Uniform cut, apron type, action, expression, room details, light and camera are replaceable authorial choices. The test plan is an experiment criterion, not an expansion of requester locks.','All 31 distinct sources and 33 query occurrences were read in full, including bilingual propositions, native conditions/effects and metadata boundaries. New school-appearance sources have native_approval=false/not_qualified; research metadata never grants adoption.','', '## B0 independent baseline','',base,'','B0 assessment: the garment change follows the completed practical; visible flour and bread make the action understandable, two hands share a single physical target, and a small smile remains directed toward the result. Its disadvantage is that a waist knot can demand careful pixel scale; the knees-up frontal view is chosen to preserve it while retaining face and school context. Face resemblance is assessable but not identity proof.','']
for oid,text in options.items():
 cid,dimensions,judgment=assess[oid]
 lines+=['## '+oid,'','Source cue(s): '+cid,'Changed open dimensions: '+dimensions+'. Source cues remain review material; this alternative is not native qualification or adopted output.','',text,'','Comparison using fidelity, required legibility, subject presence, situation, connected cause-response, emotional credibility, hierarchy and the same controls: '+judgment,'']
lines+=['## Final selection','','B0 is selected unchanged after the seven complete alternatives above. Its paired garment action and completed work tell one coherent moment. None of the alternatives earns a retained local effect; no candidate is adopted, and the fact that new school-appearance data was exposed is reported separately from influence. This is an independent preference judgment, not proof of future pixels or user acceptance.','', '## Complete-source decisions','']
for r in reviews:lines += [f"### {r['review_id']} {r['candidate_id']} / {r['realization_id']}",f"Source SHA-256: {r['source_sha256']}; queries: {', '.join(r['queries'])}",r['complete_source_review'],'Final: skip; no native adoption.','']
(b/'composition-comparison.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
review=json.loads((b/'embodiment_review.json').read_text());review['provenance']='agent_postcomposition';review['summary']='After complete-source and alternative comparison, I reread the unchanged complete prompt. One standing fictional human wearer has both hands at her own front apron waist knot, left steadying and right pulling a loose end; the neck strap continues supporting the bib as the waist tie slackens. Both forearms and the tray remain separated in the planned frontal view.'
composed={'pack_id':p['pack_id'],'global_retrieval_sha256':p['global_retrieval']['canonical_sha256'],'composer':'agent','prompt_en':base,'negative_en':p['negative_en'],'chosen_candidate_ids':[],'candidate_interpretations':[],'coverage_assertions':{x['text']:x['text'] for x in p['mandatory_intents']},'authorial_core_binding':{'source_authorial_core_sha256':p['authorial_core']['canonical_sha256'],'source_intent_lock_sha256':p['authorial_core']['intent_lock']['canonical_sha256'],'preserved_anchor_ids':[x['anchor_id'] for x in p['authorial_core']['intent_lock']['semantic_anchors']],'preserved_evidence':[],'authorial_decisions':[]},'semantic_clarification_decisions':[{'clarification_id':'clarification:authorial-core:interpreted-intent','decision':'applied','rationale':'Retain the exact narrow school-life concept, student subject and school-life moment anchors while leaving incidental staging authorial.','prompt_evidence':'Make a school-life photograph of a student character, capturing a moment of school life'}],'h_f2_material_decisions':decisions,'embodiment_review':{'source_contract_sha256':p['embodiment_preflight']['canonical_sha256'],'review':review},'adult_appeal_brief':{'adult_subject_phrase':'A fictional adult woman','agency_phrase':'Her left hand steadies the front waist knot while her right hand draws one loose tie sideways through the bow','axes':{'sensual':{'intensity':1,'realization':'baseline','affected_dimensions':[],'artistic_interpretation':'A small release of effort, unguarded task-directed presence and tactile window-lit cotton supply subtle supporting attraction. This is a proposed contextual reading, not evidence of the reference person desire or a measured image strength.','prompt_evidence':'Soft afternoon window light gives her face and rumpled cotton a tactile warmth'},'fetish':{'intensity':0,'realization':'baseline','affected_dimensions':[],'artistic_interpretation':'No added fetish treatment. The apron and fastening are functional parts of the class task.','prompt_evidence':'flour on the apron and a tray of golden bread cooling beside her connect her clothing to the work she has just finished'}},'blend':{'emphasis':'sensual_led'},'contextual_review':[],'contextual_comparison':'The contextual inventory is empty; no unreviewed contextual candidate is adopted. The same supporting attraction is considered in B0 and seven whole alternatives in composition-comparison.md. B0 ties a small relieved smile and tactile warmth to completed work; inspection, snapshot, skirt motion, lantern and stretch variants redirect that relationship without a better whole-image result.'}}
